# Symphony Elixir — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# The .env file is loaded automatically from the WORKFLOW.md directory at startup.
# Existing environment variables always take precedence over .env values.
#
# .env and .env.* are gitignored — your secrets will not be committed.

# ─── Tracker: Linear ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required when tracker.kind is "linear" in WORKFLOW.md.
# Used for authenticating with the Linear GraphQL API.
#
# How to obtain:
#   Linear → Settings → Security & access → Personal API keys → Create key
#
# LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional. Filter issues to only those assigned to this user.
# Set to "me" to auto-resolve via the API, or a Linear user UUID.
#
# LINEAR_ASSIGNEE=me

# ─── Tracker: GitHub ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required when tracker.kind is "github" in WORKFLOW.md.
# Used for authenticating with the GitHub REST API.
#
# How to obtain:
#   GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens → Fine-grained tokens
#   Required permissions: Issues (read/write) on the target repository
#   Classic tokens with "repo" scope also work.
#
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional. Filter issues to only those assigned to this GitHub username.
# Set to "me" to auto-resolve via GET /user, or a literal GitHub login.
#
# GITHUB_ASSIGNEE=me

# ─── Workspace ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Override the workspace root directory where Symphony creates per-issue workspaces.
# Can also be set via tracker.workspace.root in WORKFLOW.md using $SYMPHONY_WORKSPACE_ROOT.
# Default: system temp directory / symphony_workspaces
#
# SYMPHONY_WORKSPACE_ROOT=~/code/symphony-workspaces

# ─── Codex ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Override the Codex binary path or command.
# Can be referenced in WORKFLOW.md codex.command as "$CODEX_BIN app-server".
# Default (if not set): "codex app-server"
#
# CODEX_BIN=codex

# ─── Display ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Override terminal width for the status dashboard.
# Only affects the terminal-based dashboard rendering, not the Phoenix LiveView.
# Default: auto-detected from terminal
#
# COLUMNS=120
